Southstar for Debian: the crates.io dependencies
=================================================

Southstar is a Cargo workspace whose Cargo.lock pins its crates.io
dependencies (rustls, ring, wasmi, png, ...). They are not part of the
upstream tree, and an sbuild/pbuilder chroot has no network, so a source
package carries them as a second orig tarball that unpacks into vendor/:

    cargo vendor --locked vendor
    tar -cJf ../southstar_<version>.orig-vendor.tar.xz vendor

dpkg-source unpacks the component next to debian/, and debian/rules then
points cargo at it (CARGO_HOME=debian/cargo-home with a source replacement for
crates-io, CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true). Without vendor/ the build fetches the
crates from crates.io, which works for a binary build on a networked machine:

    dpkg-buildpackage -b -uc -us

Regenerate the component whenever Cargo.lock changes. debian/rules only
looks for a vendor/ directory, so it works unchanged if the crates are ever
committed to the tree instead (decision D4 in docs/rust-port.md).

Rust 1.91 or newer is required. Debian forky and sid package it (rustc and
cargo 1.96 and 1.97). Ubuntu 24.04 ships it as the versioned rustc-1.91 and
cargo-1.91 packages, which Build-Depends accepts as alternatives and
debian/rules puts first on PATH. sbuild considers only the first alternative
unless told otherwise, so build for Ubuntu with --resolve-alternatives:

    sbuild --resolve-alternatives -d noble

With a rustup toolchain instead, build with dpkg-buildpackage -d, which skips
the Build-Depends check for cargo and rustc; rust-toolchain.toml selects
1.91.0 inside the tree.
